+    // instantiated under NEVER_UPDATE (which keeps stable command-buffer-visible
+    // addresses, so buffers captured at record time stay resident) accumulate
+    // graph-pool memory that is never reclaimed -- a large VRAM leak that
+    // survives process teardown and even GPU reset on ROCm 7.14. Trim the
+    // device graph mem pool after destroying the exec so its backing memory is
+    // returned. `hipDeviceGraphMemTrim` takes a device ordinal (no need to set
+    // the current device) and is a no-op when the pool is already empty.
